<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Local Areas</span>
<h1>Soc Son by Motorbike: Motorbike Traffic Guide in Hanoi</h1>
<p>Soc Son is Hanoi&rsquo;s northern gateway, the half-rural district at the top of the city where the roads open out, the villages keep their own pace and the traffic is a different animal from the centre&rsquo;s, lighter, faster between the towns and organised by the airport&rsquo;s rhythm rather than the market&rsquo;s. A rider based here meets the open-road version of Hanoi, long clear stretches, big vehicles on the through routes and the small surprises of village traffic, and the skill the district asks is the planner&rsquo;s small one, respecting speed and distance the way the dense grid never demands. This page reads that character without live-traffic claims, because flow is a fact of the day and the hour, and the guide that quotes numbers for it is guessing in a confident voice.</p>
<p>The rental counter is at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, across the river on the city&rsquo;s eastern side, so the traffic education begins with the long northern run from pickup. Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the machines and verified prices at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, browse the wider <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>, read the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/soc-son-rental-planning/">Soc Son rental planning</a> page for the base-first picture, and see the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/bac-tu-liem-traffic-guide/">Bac Tu Liem traffic guide</a> for the district on the southern run&rsquo;s way.</p>
